[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m [response] Let's denote the three consecutive integers as \(n-1\), \(n\), and \(n+1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m First, we know that the product of these three integers is 120:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m (n-1) \cdot n \cdot (n+1) = 120
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Next, we calculate the mean of these three integers:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \text{Mean} = \frac{(n-1) + n + (n+1)}{3} = \frac{3n}{3} = n
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m According to the problem, the product of the three integers divided by their mean is 24:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \frac{(n-1) \cdot n \cdot (n+1)}{n} = 24
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Simplifying the left-hand side:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
