[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Thus,
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \frac{(n^2 - 1) \cdot n}{n} = n^2 - 1 = 24
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Solving for \(n\):
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m n^2 - 1 = 24 \implies n^2 = 25 \implies n = 5 \quad (\text{since } n \text{ must be a positive integer})
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Therefore, the three consecutive integers are \(4\), \(5\), and \(6\). The largest of these integers is:
