[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m The first term of the arithmetic sequence $A$ is $5$, and the common difference is $-2$. Therefore, the $k^{th}$ term of $A$ can be expressed as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[ a_k = 5 + (k-1)(-2) = 5 - 2(k-1) = 7 - 2k. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Now, the $k^{th}$ term of the sequence $B$ is defined as $2$ raised to the $k^{th}$ term of $A$. So, the $k^{th}$ term of $B$ is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[ b_k = 2^{a_k} = 2^{7-2k}. \]
