[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m [response] To solve this problem, we need to calculate the probability of winning the game before the fourth turn. The game is won if, on any given turn, a standard die shows a 1 or a 6 (which happens with a probability of \( \frac{2}{6} = \frac{1}{3} \)) and a fair coin shows heads (which happens with a probability of \( \frac{1}{2} \)). Therefore, the probability of winning on any given turn is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[ P(\text{win}) = \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{6} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Consequently, the probability of not winning on any given turn is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
