[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m [response] To solve this problem, we need to find how many pots are marked with all three colors: red, blue, and yellow. A pot will have all three colors if it is a multiple of 4, 6, and 10 simultaneously. The least common multiple (LCM) of these numbers will give us the interval at which a pot is marked with all three colors.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m First, let's find the LCM of 4, 6, and 10.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - The prime factorization of 4 is \(2^2\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - The prime factorization of 6 is \(2 \times 3\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - The prime factorization of 10 is \(2 \times 5\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
