[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[s = 7\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m When the square is folded so that one pair of opposite corners coincide, the fold line is the diagonal of the square. This diagonal divides the square into two congruent right-angled isosceles triangles. The legs of these triangles are the sides of the square, and the hypotenuse is the diagonal of the square.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m The length of the diagonal $d$ of a square with side length $s$ can be found using the Pythagorean theorem:
