[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m [response] The probability of winning on any given turn is the product of the probability of rolling a 1 or 6 on a die and the probability of the coin showing heads. The probability of rolling a 1 or 6 on a standard die is $\frac{2}{6} = \frac{1}{3}$, and the probability of the coin showing heads is $\frac{1}{2}$. Therefore, the probability of winning on any given turn is $\frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{6}$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m The probability of not winning on a given turn is $1 - \frac{1}{6} = \frac{5}{6}$. The probability of not winning on the first three turns is $\left(\frac{5}{6}\right)^3$. Therefore, the probability of winning before the fourth turn is $1 - \left(\frac{5}{6}\right)^3$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Calculating this, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[1 - \left(\frac{5}{6}\right)^3 = 1 - \frac{125}{216} = \frac{216 - 125}{216} = \frac{91}{216}\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
