[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m The perimeter of one of these triangles is the sum of the lengths of its three sides. The two legs are each $7$ inches, and the hypotenuse, which is the diagonal of the square, can be found using the Pythagorean theorem: $d = \sqrt{7^2 + 7^2} = \sqrt{49 + 49} = \sqrt{98} = 7\sqrt{2}$ inches.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
