[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m The probability of not winning on a turn is $1 - \frac{1}{6} = \frac{5}{6}$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m The probability of winning before the fourth turn is the sum of the probabilities of winning on the first, second, or third turn. This can be calculated as follows:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - Winning on the first turn: $\frac{1}{6}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - Winning on the second turn (but not on the first): $\frac{5}{6} \times \frac{1}{6}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - Winning on the third turn (but not on the first or second): $\left(\frac{5}{6}\right)^2 \times \frac{1}{6}$
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Adding these probabilities together, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \frac{1}{6} + \frac{5}{6} \times \frac{1}{6} + \left(\frac{5}{6}\right)^2 \times \frac{1}{6} = \frac{1}{6} + \frac{5}{36} + \frac{25}{216} = \frac{36}{216} + \frac{30}{216} + \frac{25}{216} = \frac{91}{216}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Thus, the probability the game will be won before the fourth turn is $\boxed{\frac{91}{216}}$.
