[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m [response] Let the three consecutive integers be \(n-1\), \(n\), and \(n+1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Given that their product is 120:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m (n-1)n(n+1) = 120
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m The mean of the three integers is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \frac{(n-1) + n + (n+1)}{3} = \frac{3n}{3} = n
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m According to the problem, the product divided by the mean is 24:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \frac{(n-1)n(n+1)}{n} = 24
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
