[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - \(n\) is the number of times that interest is compounded per year.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - \(t\) is the time the money is invested for, in years.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Given:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - \(P = 10000\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - \(r = 0.045\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - \(n = 1\) (since interest is compounded annually)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m - \(t = 2\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m Substituting these values into the formula:
