[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m [response] To solve this, we first calculate the probability of winning on any given turn. The probability of rolling a 1 or 6 on a die is \(\frac{2}{6} = \frac{1}{3}\). The probability of getting heads on a coin is \(\frac{1}{2}\). Thus, the probability of winning on any turn is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=1936665)[0m \frac{1}{3} \times \frac{1}{2} = \frac{1}{6}
